The parent of the preforked children (-c, more than one) looped in its SIGCHLD handler:
waitpid(WNOHANG) answers 0 while other children are alive, and the loop ran until -1 (100%
of a CPU in the parent after the first child ended). The loop ends when it reaped none.
Upstream after 1.1.0 (2041deb, 09.01.2014, gnosek/fcgiwrap#18), in the snapshot Gentoo
takes (www-misc/fcgiwrap 1.1.0_p20150419).

--- fcgiwrap.c.orig
+++ fcgiwrap.c
@@ -639,7 +639,7 @@
 {
 	int status;
 
-	while ((dummy = waitpid(-1, &status, WNOHANG)) != -1) {
+	while ((dummy = waitpid(-1, &status, WNOHANG)) > 0) {
 		/* sanity check */
 		if (nrunning > 0)
 			nrunning--;
